### Generate Text with Compatible Zod Schema (OpenAI, TypeScript)

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/09-troubleshooting/20-no-object-generated-content-filter.mdx

This snippet shows the correct way to define a Zod schema for OpenAI structured output by using `.nullable()` instead of `.nullish()` or `.optional()` to avoid `NoObjectGeneratedError`.

```typescript
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai';
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { z } from 'zod';

// Correct approach - use .nullable()
const result = await generateText({
  model: openai('gpt-4o-2024-08-06'),
  output: Output.object({
    schema: z.object({
      name: z.string().nullable(), // 
      email: z.string().nullable(), // 
      age: z.number().nullable(),
    }),
  }),
  prompt: 'Generate a user profile',
});

console.log(result.output);
// { name: "John Doe", email: "john@example.com", age: 30 }
// or { name: null, email: null, age: 25 }
```

--------------------------------

### Generate Structured JSON Data with AI SDK and Zod

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/cookbook/00-guides/24-o3.mdx

Use `Output.object` with a Zod schema to constrain the model's output to a specific, type-safe JSON structure.

```ts
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai';
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { z } from 'zod';

const { output } = await generateText({
  model: openai('o3-mini'),
  output: Output.object({
    schema: z.object({
      recipe: z.object({
        name: z.string(),
        ingredients: z.array(
          z.object({ name: z.string(), amount: z.string() }),
        ),
        steps: z.array(z.string()),
      }),
    }),
  }),
  prompt: 'Generate a lasagna recipe.',
});
```

--------------------------------

### Output.object({ schema })

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/03-ai-sdk-core/10-generating-structured-data.mdx

Configures generation to produce a structured object conforming to a provided schema (e.g., Zod schema). Output is type-validated against the schema.

```APIDOC
### Function: `Output.object({ schema })`

#### Description
Specifies that the model should generate a structured object based on a validation schema.

#### Parameters
- **schema** (`Schema<T>`) - Required - Schema (such as a Zod schema) defining the structure and types of the expected output object.

#### Returns
An output specification that produces a validated object matching the schema.

#### Example
```ts
import { generateText, Output } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

const { output } = await generateText({
  output: Output.object({
    schema: z.object({
      name: z.string(),
      age: z.number().nullable(),
      labels: z.array(z.string()),
    }),
  }),
  prompt: 'Generate information for a test user.',
});
```
```

--------------------------------

### Import default OpenAI provider instance

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/providers/01-ai-sdk-providers/03-openai.mdx

Import the pre-configured default `openai` provider instance from `@ai-sdk/openai`.

```ts
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
```

### Object generation failed with OpenAI > Solution

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/09-troubleshooting/20-no-object-generated-content-filter.mdx

To resolve this issue, replace .nullish() and .optional() with .nullable() in your Zod schemas when performing structured output generation with OpenAI models.

